# vis kind=w act=x_px_hook time=night money=1 kick="THE IF MACHINE · A THOUGHT EXPERIMENT" head="WHAT IF MONEY|*DISAPPEARED?*"
What if, tonight, every coin, every banknote and every number in every bank account
simply disappeared, not stolen, just gone?

# vis kind=w act=x_px_chapter n=1 obj=scale head="WHAT MONEY|*REALLY DOES*"
To see what would go missing, it helps to start with a simple question.

# vis kind=w act=x_px_barter kick="THE DOUBLE COINCIDENCE OF WANTS" head="THE BARTER|*PROBLEM*" k=2
Imagine you raise cows and you want rice.
You would need someone who has rice and wants a cow, today.
And the two of you would still have to agree on a price.

# vis kind=w act=x_px_signal kick="JOB 3 OF MONEY" head="A PRICE IS|A *MESSAGE*"
When bread runs short, its price goes up,
and that tells bakers to bake more and shoppers to buy a little less.

# vis kind=w act=x_px_queue kick="ANSWER 1 · THE QUEUE" head="FREE COSTS|*TIME*" k=1
When something is free and everyone wants it, people line up for it,
and you end up paying with your time instead of your money.

# vis kind=w act=x_px_parcel kick="PRISONER-OF-WAR CAMPS · 1940s" head="WHAT CAME IN|THE *PARCEL*"
Red Cross parcels arrived with food, chocolate, soap and cigarettes,
and very quickly people began to trade them.

# vis kind=w act=x_px_reborn kick="9000 BC → TODAY" head="MONEY KEEPS|*COMING BACK*" k=1
Take money away from people and they invent it again,
often within weeks.

# vis kind=w act=x_px_quote kick="WHAT IS ACTUALLY KNOWN" q="No example of a barter economy, pure and simple, has ever been described." by="CAROLINE HUMPHREY, 1985"
But the anthropologist Caroline Humphrey put it bluntly.
No example of a barter economy, pure and simple, has ever been described.

# vis kind=w act=x_px_stat kick="FINLAND · 2017–2018" head="FREE MONEY,|*SAME WORK*" v=2000 unit="unemployed people, 560 € a month" n=100 note="EACH FIGURE = 20 PEOPLE"
In Finland, two thousand unemployed people received 560 euros a month for two years,
and their employment ended up about the same.

# vis kind=w act=x_px_promise kick="WHAT MONEY REALLY IS" head="A SHARED|*PROMISE*" k=1
A banknote is paper and an account is a number,
so what is real is the trust behind them, a promise millions of strangers keep.
